--- # State Management Guidelines

## Scope / Flexibility Notice
These guidelines establish standards for application state management, with the BLoC Pattern as the primary method. These principles ensure unidirectional data flow, high testability, and clear separation between UI and business logic.

## Best Practices
- Implement unidirectional data flow: State → UI → Events → State
- Keep presentation layer free of business logic
- Design states as immutable objects with equality comparisons
- Use domain layer use cases as dependencies for BLoCs
- Clearly define boundaries between state types (UI state vs Business state)
- Avoid storing state in widgets; always use BLoC or other state management mechanisms
- Optimize widget rebuilds using selective builders
- Handle errors and loading states consistently throughout the application
- Encapsulate business logic in use cases and repositories, not in BLoC
- Provide debouncing and throttling for events that need it

## File / Project Structure Guidelines
- BLoC directory structure:
  ```
  lib/
    presentation/
      blocs/
        feature_name/
          feature_bloc.dart        # BLoC class definition  
          feature_event.dart       # Events as sealed class
          feature_state.dart       # States as sealed class
  ```

- Example of BLoC file structure:
  ```dart
  // chat_bloc.dart
  class ChatBloc extends Bloc<ChatEvent, ChatState> {
    final GetMessages _getMessages;
    final SendMessage _sendMessage;
    
    ChatBloc({
      required GetMessages getMessages,
      required SendMessage sendMessage,
    }) : _getMessages = getMessages,
         _sendMessage = sendMessage,
         super(const ChatState.initial()) {
      on<ChatLoadEvent>(_onChatLoad);
      on<ChatSendMessageEvent>(_onChatSendMessage);
    }
    
    Future<void> _onChatLoad(ChatLoadEvent event, Emitter<ChatState> emit) async {
      // Implementation
    }
  }
  ```

## Event & State Design
- Event design:
  ```dart
  @freezed
  class ChatEvent with _$ChatEvent {
    const factory ChatEvent.load({required String chatId}) = ChatLoadEvent;
    const factory ChatEvent.sendMessage({
      required String content,
      required MessageType type,
    }) = ChatSendMessageEvent;
    const factory ChatEvent.messageReceived({required Message message}) = ChatMessageReceivedEvent;
  }
  ```

- State design:
  ```dart
  @freezed
  class ChatState with _$ChatState {
    const factory ChatState.initial() = _Initial;
    const factory ChatState.loading() = _Loading;
    const factory ChatState.loaded({
      required List<Message> messages,
      required bool isTyping,
    }) = _Loaded;
    const factory ChatState.error({required String message}) = _Error;
  }
  ```

## Clean Architecture Integration
- BLoCs depend only on domain layer (use cases), never directly on data layer
- Use cases return only domain entities, never data models
- BLoCs transform domain entities into state objects when needed
- Use Result or Either for error handling in use cases:
  ```dart
  class SendMessage {
    final MessageRepository _repository;
    
    SendMessage(this._repository);
    
    Future<Either<Failure, Message>> call(String content, String chatId) async {
      // Implementation
    }
  }
  
  // In BLoC:
  final result = await _sendMessage(event.content, _chatId);
  result.fold(
    (failure) => emit(ChatState.error(message: failure.message)),
    (message) => emit(ChatState.loaded(messages: [...state.messages, message], isTyping: false)),
  );
  ```

## BLoC + Services Integration
- Integration with background services:
  ```dart
  class NotificationBloc extends Bloc<NotificationEvent, NotificationState> {
    final NotificationService _notificationService;
    late final StreamSubscription<NotificationData> _subscription;
    
    NotificationBloc({required NotificationService notificationService})
        : _notificationService = notificationService,
          super(const NotificationState.initial()) {
      _subscription = _notificationService.notifications.listen(_onNotificationReceived);
      on<NotificationReceivedEvent>(_onNotificationEvent);
    }
    
    void _onNotificationReceived(NotificationData data) {
      add(NotificationEvent.received(data));
    }
    
    @override
    Future<void> close() {
      _subscription.cancel();
      return super.close();
    }
  }
  ```

- Integration with real-time messaging:
  ```dart
  class MessageBloc extends Bloc<MessageEvent, MessageState> {
    final ChatService _chatService;
    late final StreamSubscription<Message> _messageSubscription;
    
    MessageBloc({required ChatService chatService}) 
        : _chatService = chatService,
          super(const MessageState.initial()) {
      _messageSubscription = _chatService.messageStream.listen(_onMessageReceived);
      on<MessageReceivedEvent>(_onMessageEvent);
    }
    
    void _onMessageReceived(Message message) {
      add(MessageEvent.received(message));
    }
    
    @override
    Future<void> close() {
      _messageSubscription.cancel();
      return super.close();
    }
  }
  ```

## Coding & Styling Conventions
- Use freezed to create sealed classes for events and states
- Implement copyWith methods for all state classes
- Mark state classes with @immutable
- Use extension methods for state objects when utility methods are needed:
  ```dart
  extension ChatStateX on ChatState {
    bool get isLoading => maybeMap(
      loading: (_) => true,
      orElse: () => false,
    );
    
    List<Message> get messages => maybeMap(
      loaded: (state) => state.messages,
      orElse: () => [],
    );
  }
  ```
- Name BLoCs by related feature: `ChatBloc`, `AuthBloc`
- Name Events with action phrases: `ChatLoadEvent`, `ChatSendMessageEvent`
- Name States descriptively: `ChatLoadedState`, `ChatLoadingState`

## Performance & Optimization Tips
- Use `equatable` or `freezed` for efficient state comparison
- Use selective builders to limit rebuilds:
  ```dart
  BlocSelector<ChatBloc, ChatState, bool>(
    selector: (state) => state.isLoading,
    builder: (context, isLoading) {
      return isLoading ? const LoadingIndicator() : const SizedBox();
    },
  );
  ```
- Use `buildWhen` in `BlocBuilder` to rebuild only when necessary:
  ```dart
  BlocBuilder<ChatBloc, ChatState>(
    buildWhen: (prev, current) => prev.messages != current.messages,
    builder: (context, state) => MessageList(messages: state.messages),
  );
  ```
- Avoid emitting state when there's no change
- Implement distinction to prevent duplicate emissions:
  ```dart
  on<ChatLoadEvent>(
    (event, emit) async {
      // Avoid emitting loading if already loading
      if (state is! ChatLoadingState) {
        emit(const ChatState.loading());
      }
    },
    transformer: distinct(), // Prevent duplicate events
  );
  ```

## Cubit Integration
- Cubit is a simplified version of BLoC that doesn't require events
- Use Cubit for simpler features alongside BLoC for complex ones
- Directory structure for Cubits:
  ```
  lib/
    presentation/
      cubits/
        feature_name/
          feature_cubit.dart        # Cubit class definition
          feature_state.dart        # States as sealed class (if needed)
  ```

- Example of Cubit file structure:
  ```dart
  // counter_cubit.dart
  class CounterCubit extends Cubit<int> {
    CounterCubit() : super(0);
    
    void increment() => emit(state + 1);
    void decrement() => emit(state - 1);
    void reset() => emit(0);
  }
  ```

- Example with complex state:
  ```dart
  // todo_cubit.dart
  class TodoCubit extends Cubit<TodoState> {
    final GetTodos _getTodos;
    final AddTodo _addTodo;
    
    TodoCubit({
      required GetTodos getTodos,
      required AddTodo addTodo,
    }) : _getTodos = getTodos,
         _addTodo = addTodo,
         super(const TodoState.initial());
    
    Future<void> loadTodos() async {
      emit(state.copyWith(isLoading: true, errorMessage: null));
      
      final result = await _getTodos();
      result.fold(
        (failure) => emit(state.copyWith(
          isLoading: false, 
          errorMessage: failure.message
        )),
        (todos) => emit(state.copyWith(
          todos: todos, 
          isLoading: false
        )),
      );
    }
    
    Future<void> addNewTodo(String title, String description) async {
      emit(state.copyWith(isSubmitting: true));
      
      final todo = Todo(
        id: DateTime.now().toString(),
        title: title,
        description: description,
        isCompleted: false,
      );
      
      final result = await _addTodo(todo);
      result.fold(
        (failure) => emit(state.copyWith(
          isSubmitting: false, 
          errorMessage: failure.message
        )),
        (_) {
          final updatedTodos = [...state.todos, todo];
          emit(state.copyWith(
            todos: updatedTodos,
            isSubmitting: false,
          ));
        },
      );
    }
  }
  ```
  
- Using Cubits with widgets:
  ```dart
  BlocProvider(
    create: (context) => getIt<TodoCubit>()..loadTodos(),
    child: BlocConsumer<TodoCubit, TodoState>(
      listener: (context, state) {
        if (state.errorMessage != null) {
          ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(
            SnackBar(content: Text(state.errorMessage!)),
          );
        }
      },
      builder: (context, state) {
        if (state.isLoading) {
          return const Center(child: CircularProgressIndicator());
        }
        
        return TodoList(todos: state.todos);
      },
    ),
  );
  ```

## Choosing Between BLoC and Cubit

### Use Cubit When:
- State changes are direct and simple
- You don't need explicit events
- You prefer less boilerplate code
- For simpler features or components
- When team members are newer to reactive patterns

### Use BLoC When:
- You need to track or transform events
- Multiple events can lead to the same state
- The feature has complex business logic
- When you need more structured state transitions
- For application-wide state with multi-screen impact

### Hybrid Approach Best Practices
- Use consistent dependency injection for both
- Follow the same naming patterns
- Place in similarly structured directories
- Test with the same level of coverage
- Document why you chose Cubit or BLoC for each feature
- Maintain consistent error handling approaches ## Testing & Validation Guidelines
- Test each event handler in the BLoC individually
- Use bloc_test to test state sequences:
  ```dart
  blocTest<ChatBloc, ChatState>(
    'emits [loading, loaded] when messages are loaded successfully',
    build: () {
      when(() => mockGetMessages(any()))
          .thenAnswer((_) async => Right([testMessage]));
      return ChatBloc(getMessages: mockGetMessages, sendMessage: mockSendMessage);
    },
    act: (bloc) => bloc.add(const ChatEvent.load(chatId: '123')),
    expect: () => [
      const ChatState.loading(),
      ChatState.loaded(messages: [testMessage], isTyping: false),
    ],
    verify: (_) {
      verify(() => mockGetMessages('123')).called(1);
    },
  );
  ```
- Test error handling in BLoCs:
  ```dart
  blocTest<ChatBloc, ChatState>(
    'emits [loading, error] when message loading fails',
    build: () {
      when(() => mockGetMessages(any()))
          .thenAnswer((_) async => Left(NetworkFailure('Connection error')));
      return ChatBloc(getMessages: mockGetMessages, sendMessage: mockSendMessage);
    },
    act: (bloc) => bloc.add(const ChatEvent.load(chatId: '123')),
    expect: () => [
      const ChatState.loading(),
      const ChatState.error(message: 'Connection error'),
    ],
  );
  ```
- Test integration with services and streams:
  ```dart
  test('subscribes to notification stream on creation', () {
    // Arrange
    final controller = StreamController<NotificationData>();
    when(() => mockNotificationService.notifications).thenAnswer((_) => controller.stream);
    
    // Act
    final bloc = NotificationBloc(notificationService: mockNotificationService);
    controller.add(testNotification);
    
    // Assert
    verify(() => mockNotificationService.notifications).called(1);
    expectLater(
      bloc.stream,
      emits(NotificationState.received(notification: testNotification)),
    );
  });
  ```